## File written

`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/skill-graph/skill-graph-db.ts` (only file touched by me)

- `loadSkillEmbeddings(skillIds?)` — active-pointer branch now computes the skill rows into `skillRows` and returns `appendCommandEmbeddingRows(...)`. The existing skill SELECT/map/decode/filter code is byte-identical, just bound to a name. The `vec_<dim>`-missing early return now feeds `[]` as the skill rows into the same helper, so an id list can still find command rows.
- New module-private `appendCommandEmbeddingRows(database, dim, skillIds, skillRows, hasTable)` placed after the function, matching the file's "helper follows its caller" precedent: returns `skillRows` unchanged when no ids are passed, when the `vec_cmd_<dim>` table is absent, or when the read throws (that last case logs one `[skill-graph] Command embedding load failed; command rows omitted (...)` warning). Otherwise it selects `command_id IN (...)` from the sibling table, maps `command_id → skillId` in the same `SkillEmbeddingRow` shape, and appends.
- Legacy `skill_nodes.embedding` fallback path untouched (no active dim exists on that branch, so there is no sibling table name to derive).
- Comment prose carries only the durable WHY: no spec path, phase, task id, ADR/REQ, em dash, or semicolon.

